---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/ui/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import PageIntro from '../../components/ui/PageIntro.astro';
import SwpCalculatorIsland from '../../features/calculators/SwpCalculatorIsland';
import { getBreadcrumbsForPath } from '../../config/routes';

const crumbs = getBreadcrumbsForPath('/tools/swp/');
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Systematic Withdrawal Plan (SWP) Cash-Flow Simulator — Ant Wealth Creation"
  description="Model monthly cash outflows, capital longevity, and balance depletion from an invested mutual fund corpus."
  currentPath="/tools/swp/"
>
  <div class="container page-container">
    <Breadcrumbs crumbs={crumbs} />

    <PageIntro
      eyebrow="Cash-Flow Modeling"
      title="Systematic Withdrawal Plan (SWP) Simulator"
      description="Plan regular monthly cash flows from an accumulated corpus. Model portfolio longevity, withdrawal rates, annual step-ups, and balance trajectory."
      statusBadge="Interactive Calculator Active • 50-Year Simulation"
    />

    <!-- Interactive Concept C SWP Longevity Simulator Island -->
    <SwpCalculatorIsland client:load />

    <!-- Key Dynamics of SWP -->
    <section class="educational-insight-box" aria-labelledby="insight-heading">
      <h2 id="insight-heading" class="section-title">Key Dynamics of Systematic Withdrawal Planning</h2>
      <p class="section-desc">
        In decumulation planning, sustainability is sensitive to withdrawal rate, market volatility, inflation, and sequence-of-returns risk:
      </p>

      <div class="swp-rules-grid">
        <div class="swp-card safe-rule">
          <span class="swp-badge">Illustrative Benchmark</span>
          <div class="swp-metric">4% – 6% Initial Withdrawal Assumption</div>
          <p class="swp-desc">In financial planning scenarios, an initial annual withdrawal rate between 4% and 6% is frequently modeled as an illustrative stress test. Actual portfolio longevity depends on realized asset returns, volatility sequence, and inflation.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="swp-card danger-rule">
          <span class="swp-badge">Elevated Depletion Risk</span>
          <div class="swp-metric">&gt; 8%–9% Annual Withdrawal Assumption</div>
          <p class="swp-desc">Higher withdrawal rates combined with early market downturns (negative sequence of returns) substantially accelerate capital erosion and can lead to premature portfolio exhaustion.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Structural SWP Principles -->
    <section class="principles-section" aria-labelledby="principles-heading">
      <h2 id="principles-heading" class="section-title">Fundamental Mechanics of Mutual Fund SWP</h2>
      <p class="section-desc">
        Unlike bank fixed-deposit interest payouts, a Systematic Withdrawal Plan in mutual funds operates on unit cancellation:
      </p>

      <div class="principles-grid">
        <div class="principle-card">
          <div class="principle-icon" aria-hidden="true">🔢</div>
          <h3 class="principle-title">Unit Redemption vs Interest</h3>
          <p class="principle-desc">
            An SWP generates monthly cash flow by redeeming the exact number of units required to equal your desired rupee amount at prevailing NAV. When NAV rises, fewer units are redeemed; when NAV declines, more units are redeemed.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="principle-card">
          <div class="principle-icon" aria-hidden="true">⚖️</div>
          <h3 class="principle-title">Capital Preservation vs Depletion</h3>
          <p class="principle-desc">
            If your withdrawal rate is lower than the net portfolio return, your underlying capital continues to compound. If your withdrawal rate exceeds portfolio return plus inflation, your capital base gradually depletes.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="principle-card">
          <div class="principle-icon" aria-hidden="true">🗓️</div>
          <h3 class="principle-title">Timing: Beginning vs End of Period</h3>
          <p class="principle-desc">
            Withdrawal timing mathematically influences compounding. Withdrawing at the beginning of each month (annuity due) leaves slightly less capital to compound during that month compared to end-of-month withdrawals.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Indian Mutual Fund SWP Taxation Primer -->
    <section class="tax-primer-section" aria-labelledby="tax-heading">
      <div class="tax-primer-box">
        <h2 id="tax-heading" class="tax-title">Indian Mutual Fund SWP Taxation Primer</h2>
        <p class="tax-desc">
          One of the major advantages of mutual fund SWP compared to traditional bank deposits is its tax efficiency, governed by the First-In, First-Out (FIFO) principle:
        </p>
        <ul class="tax-list">
          <li><strong>Principal vs Gain Separation:</strong> In each SWP withdrawal, only the capital gains component is taxable; the principal invested is returned tax-free. In early years of an SWP, principal constitutes a large portion of the redemption.</li>
          <li><strong>Equity Mutual Funds (Section 112A):</strong> Long-term capital gains (held &gt; 12 months) are taxed at 12.5% on gains exceeding the statutory ₹1.25 Lakh threshold per financial year. Short-term gains are taxed at 20% (Section 111A).</li>
          <li><strong>Debt Mutual Funds (Section 50AA):</strong> For specified debt funds acquired after 1 April 2023, capital gains are treated as short-term and taxed at the investor's applicable income tax slab rate.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="tax-footer">
          Because tax implications depend on scheme categories, individual holding periods, and slab rates, calculating personalized net post-tax cash flows requires consultation with a qualified tax advisor.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Related Active Calculators -->
    <section class="related-tools-section" aria-labelledby="tools-heading">
      <h2 id="tools-heading" class="section-title">Explore Active Investment Calculators</h2>
      <p class="section-desc">
        Model wealth accumulation and growth using our verified interactive tools:
      </p>

      <div class="tools-grid">
        <a href="/tools/sip/" class="tool-card-link">
          <span class="tool-tag">Live Calculator</span>
          <h3 class="tool-card-title">SIP Wealth Simulator</h3>
          <p class="tool-card-desc">Explore how disciplined monthly investing compounds over multi-year horizons with verified math.</p>
          <span class="tool-card-action">Launch SIP Calculator →</span>
        </a>

        <a href="/tools/sip-growth/" class="tool-card-link">
          <span class="tool-tag">Live Calculator</span>
          <h3 class="tool-card-title">Advanced SIP Growth</h3>
          <p class="tool-card-desc">Simulate multi-lump-sum inflows, annual step-ups, and extended holding periods.</p>
          <span class="tool-card-action">Launch Advanced SIP →</span>
        </a>

        <a href="/plan/retirement-income/" class="tool-card-link">
          <span class="tool-tag">Live Planner</span>
          <h3 class="tool-card-title">Three-Bucket Framework</h3>
          <p class="tool-card-desc">Learn how to divide your retirement corpus into Liquidity, Income, and Growth buckets to manage sequence risk.</p>
          <span class="tool-card-action">Launch 3-Bucket Planner →</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="nav-links-strip">
      <a href="/tools/" class="btn-subtle">← Back to All Tools</a>
      <a href="/plan/retirement-income/" class="btn-subtle">View Three-Bucket Strategy →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-container {
    padding-bottom: var(--space-16);
  }

  .educational-insight-box,
  .principles-section,
  .tax-primer-section,
  .related-tools-section {
    margin: var(--space-12) 0;
  }

  .section-title {
    font-size: var(--text-h2);
    font-family: var(--font-family-heading);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-brand-primary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .section-desc {
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .swp-rules-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-6);
  }

  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .swp-rules-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .swp-card {
    background-color: var(--color-bg-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: var(--space-6);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-subtle);
  }

  .safe-rule {
    border-color: var(--primitive-teal-500);
    border-width: 2px;
    background-color: var(--primitive-teal-50);
  }

  .danger-rule {
    border-color: var(--primitive-rose-600);
    border-width: 2px;
    background-color: var(--primitive-rose-100);
  }

  .swp-badge {
    font-size: var(--text-caption);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-text-brand);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .swp-metric {
    font-size: var(--text-h3);
    font-family: var(--font-family-heading);
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--color-brand-primary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .swp-desc {
    font-size: var(--text-body-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .principles-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-6);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .principles-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .principle-card {
    background-color: var(--color-bg-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: var(--space-6);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }

  .principle-icon {
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    line-height: 1;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-1);
  }

  .principle-title {
    font-size: var(--text-h4);
    font-family: var(--font-family-heading);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-brand-primary);
  }

  .principle-desc {
    font-size: var(--text-body-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.55;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .tax-primer-box {
    background-color: var(--primitive-gold-50);
    border: 1px solid var(--primitive-gold-100);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--primitive-gold-500);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: var(--space-6);
  }

  .tax-title {
    font-size: var(--text-h4);
    font-family: var(--font-family-heading);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-text-accent);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .tax-desc {
    font-size: var(--text-body-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.55;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .tax-list {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4) 0;
    padding-left: var(--space-5);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    font-size: var(--text-body-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .tax-footer {
    font-size: var(--text-caption);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-text-accent);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .tools-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-6);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .tools-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .tool-card-link {
    background-color: var(--color-bg-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: var(--space-6);
    text-decoration: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    transition: transform var(--transition-fast), box-shadow var(--transition-fast), border-color var(--transition-fast);
  }

  .tool-card-link:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-subtle);
    border-color: var(--color-brand-primary);
  }

  .tool-tag {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    color: var(--color-text-brand);
    background-color: var(--primitive-teal-50);
    padding: 0.2rem 0.5rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    align-self: flex-start;
  }

  .tool-card-title {
    font-size: var(--text-h4);
    font-family: var(--font-family-heading);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-brand-primary);
  }

  .tool-card-desc {
    font-size: var(--text-body-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.5;
    flex: 1;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .tool-card-action {
    font-size: var(--text-body-sm);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-text-brand);
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }

  .nav-links-strip {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
    padding-top: var(--space-8);
    margin-top: var(--space-12);
  }

  .btn-subtle {
    font-size: var(--text-body-sm);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-text-brand);
    text-decoration: none;
    padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-4);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    transition: all var(--transition-fast);
  }

  .btn-subtle:hover {
    background-color: var(--primitive-teal-50);
    border-color: var(--primitive-teal-100);
  }
</style>
